### ============================================
### STEP 0: SETUP - Get IDs for Testing
### Run these in order, copy IDs to variables above
### ============================================

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Create a user (copy "id" from response → paste in @user_id above)
POST {{apiUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

### 3. Get existing users (alternative - copy any "id" → paste in @user_id)
GET {{apiUrl}}/users

### 4. Get a showtime (copy "id" from response → paste in @showtime_id above)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes?limit=1

### 5. Get seats for showtime (copy "id" of available seats → paste in @seat_id1, @seat_id2)
### Note: Use showtime_id from step 4, or fill @showtime_id variable first
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats 

### ============================================
### PHASE 2: Movie & Showtime Management
### ============================================

### GET /movies - List all movies
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies

### GET /movies - With filters
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies?genre=Action&language=English&limit=10

### GET /movies/{id} - Get movie details
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}

### GET /movies/{id}/showtimes - Get showtimes for movie
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}/showtimes

### GET /showtimes/{id}/seats - Get available seats
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### POST /showtimes - Create showtime
POST {{apiUrl}}/showtimes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movie_id": "{{movie_id}}",
  "screen_id": "{{screen_id}}",
  "show_time": "2024-12-20T18:00:00Z",
  "price": 12.50
}

### ============================================
### PHASE 3: Booking Endpoints (Sequential Testing)
### ============================================
### Make sure @user_id, @showtime_id, @seat_id1, @seat_id2 are filled from Step 0

### STEP 1: Reserve seats (5-minute hold)
POST {{apiUrl}}/bookings/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{user_id}}",
  "showtime_id": "{{showtime_id}}",
  "seat_ids": ["{{seat_id1}}", "{{seat_id2}}"]
}

### STEP 2: Create booking (copy "id" from response → paste in @booking_id)
POST {{apiUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{user_id}}",
  "showtime_id": "{{showtime_id}}",
  "seat_ids": ["{{seat_id1}}", "{{seat_id2}}"]
}

### STEP 3: Get booking details (use booking_id from step 2)
### NEW: Enhanced booking details with receipt format
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings/{{booking_id}}

### STEP 4: Get all bookings for user
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings/user/{{user_id}}

### STEP 4a: Enhanced booking history with filters
### Filter by status
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings/user/{{user_id}}?status=pending

### Filter by date range
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings/user/{{user_id}}?startDate=2024-01-01&endDate=2024-12-31

### Filter by status AND date range
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings/user/{{user_id}}?status=confirmed&startDate=2024-11-01&endDate=2024-11-30

### STEP 5: Get all bookings
GET {{apiUrl}}/bookings

### ============================================
### PHASE 4: Enhanced Booking Management (NEW)
### ============================================
### Make sure @booking_id is filled from STEP 2 above

### Enhanced Cancellation with Rules
### Note: Must cancel at least 2 hours before showtime
PUT {{apiUrl}}/bookings/{{booking_id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Change of plans"
}

